WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:21.456
Jon Snow.


00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.312
Oh, my goodness,
you're beautiful!


00:00:42.251 --> 00:00:45.961
- Look away. One more time, look away.
- We love your style.


00:01:01.103 --> 00:01:02.844
Hey, Sophie. Sophie.


00:01:02.938 --> 00:01:04.538
Oh, my gosh.


00:01:04.606 --> 00:01:06.438
You ready
to get down to business?


00:01:06.525 --> 00:01:08.232
You're my screensaver
on my phone!


00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:09.838
And Gwendoline, now smile here.


00:02:40.494 --> 00:02:41.701
Anna, Production.


00:02:43.246 --> 00:02:45.246
- Production, Anna speaking.
- Bear with me.


00:02:45.332 --> 00:02:48.416
Well, we do have
24-hour security at the Paint Hall.


00:02:49.086 --> 00:02:52.170
Hello. Caroline...
Got a Caroline to flip the marquee.


00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.169
Good morning.


00:02:56.885 --> 00:02:58.592
Um, the godswood recce on Friday.


00:02:59.054 --> 00:03:03.389
We need to know
exactly who is going to attend...


00:03:03.475 --> 00:03:05.495
I'd like to get shots
of you doing work.


00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:07.636
Oh, God. Doing my work.


00:03:07.729 --> 00:03:09.061
Sure.


00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:17.733
My working is putting on one pair of
glasses to the other pair of glasses.


00:03:18.323 --> 00:03:19.985
- Oh, God.
- Hi.


00:03:20.075 --> 00:03:22.783
Steve didn't respond to us
about the direwolves


00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.360
because they can go pretty fast.


00:03:24.454 --> 00:03:28.869
- He says 30 miles per hour.
- Right, right, right. Okay.


00:03:29.543 --> 00:03:31.205
So it's our biggest season ever.


00:03:31.294 --> 00:03:33.957
There's a lot of decisions
that need to be made.


00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:36.835
And something simple
like a wolf running with the guys


00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:42.387
for us means a 150-foot green screen
with a tracking vehicle in Calgary.


00:03:42.472 --> 00:03:46.091
So, you know, it's fun.
It's a fun puzzle to figure out,


00:03:46.184 --> 00:03:48.346
you know, and when you do
figure it out, it's...


00:03:48.437 --> 00:03:50.394
I think that's why
I used to love algebra,


00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:51.971
is that you'd figure out
the equation,


00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:54.523
and when you got that answer,
it was like, "Wow!"


00:03:54.609 --> 00:03:55.895
And so it's the same with this.


00:03:55.986 --> 00:04:00.777
We keep messing with the puzzle,
and then when that last piece fits,


00:04:00.866 --> 00:04:03.404
you're like, "Yeah, it worked."


00:04:03.827 --> 00:04:06.490
For you.


00:04:09.332 --> 00:04:11.574
My schedule ends up being...


00:04:11.668 --> 00:04:13.830
It's, you know, very...


00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.121
And that's a simple one.


00:04:17.883 --> 00:04:20.421
Like the Art Department,
they go horizontally,


00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:24.094
but I decided I wanted to go...
I go vertically.


00:04:26.057 --> 00:04:27.577
Do you thrive
on all of this, Chris?


00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:29.183
Not particularly.


00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:32.137
But it's all I've done
since I've left school,


00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:33.766
I don't know anything else.


00:04:39.821 --> 00:04:41.403
The way <i>Game of Thrones</i> is developed


00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:46.110
is every episode has as much in it
as any one feature film,


00:04:46.203 --> 00:04:48.741
but we have to do it quicker
and for less money.


00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:54.246
All you can do
with any large operation


00:04:54.336 --> 00:04:57.204
is get the best people around you
and let them go.


00:05:04.262 --> 00:05:06.549
Like we said before,
we're trying to figure out how...


00:05:47.722 --> 00:05:49.283
This is our first day of fittings.


00:05:49.307 --> 00:05:52.300
We're just doing 25, I think, today.


00:05:52.394 --> 00:05:54.477
We have the same people every year.


00:05:54.563 --> 00:05:58.682
It's nice, they're like a family.
They always show up every year.


00:06:01.653 --> 00:06:03.519
- Keep you nice and warm.
- Hmm.


00:06:08.743 --> 00:06:10.575
And he's obsessed
with the whole show.


00:06:10.662 --> 00:06:13.905
I think it'd be really cool if youse
got to meet him. He'd be so excited.


00:06:15.166 --> 00:06:16.998
- Hey, what?
- Hey, friend.


00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:19.459
Pat, man.


00:06:19.546 --> 00:06:20.912
- Are you Andrew?
- I am.


00:06:21.006 --> 00:06:22.900
You're the person
I'm here to see. I'm Jeanie.


00:06:22.924 --> 00:06:25.337
I'm making the documentary
about <i>Game of Thrones.</i>


00:06:25.427 --> 00:06:26.838
- Okay.
- For a whole year.


00:06:26.928 --> 00:06:28.197
- Okay.
- I was wondering


00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:29.678
if I could follow your fitting.


00:06:29.764 --> 00:06:30.845
Excellent.


00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.181
- Hello.
- I'll have you fill in that.


00:06:40.275 --> 00:06:41.641
- Thank you.
- And I'll get...


00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:45.356
- Well... Hello. How are you?
- Good to see you.


00:06:45.447 --> 00:06:48.155
- How are you? You all right?
- Nice to see you. I'm excited.


00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:49.777
- Hello.
- Are you all buzzed?


00:06:49.868 --> 00:06:52.508
- I am all buzzed. I'm all buzzed.
- You're all excited.


00:06:52.579 --> 00:06:55.242
Back in for the last season,
so I'm loving life.


00:06:59.169 --> 00:07:00.285
- Lovely.
- Yeah?


00:07:00.378 --> 00:07:01.459
Yeah.


00:07:01.546 --> 00:07:03.538
Snug.


00:07:03.632 --> 00:07:05.464
- Too snug?
- Do you want another pair?


00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.462
Could I tryjust a size bigger?


00:07:07.552 --> 00:07:10.716
Just so I can get
my thermal socks on. Cheers.


00:07:10.805 --> 00:07:13.639
As I recall, the best way into that's
on your knees, yeah?


00:07:13.725 --> 00:07:14.886
It's the easiest.


00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:17.183
That's funny.


00:07:18.188 --> 00:07:21.681
I absolutely love it, it is
the best thing I have ever seen.


00:07:21.775 --> 00:07:24.233
The stories, the characters.


00:07:24.319 --> 00:07:26.561
I read the books
since I was about 13.


00:07:26.655 --> 00:07:29.944
Absolutely brilliant, like. Honored
to be able to work on it, you know.


00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:32.150
Night King better recognize.


00:07:33.161 --> 00:07:34.722
- How you doing?
- Ah, what about you?


00:07:34.746 --> 00:07:38.205
- What about you?
- Come here. What's happening?


00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:41.079
- How's it going?
- Aye, sweet. Look at me.


00:07:41.169 --> 00:07:43.877
- Back in armor.
- Big time.


00:07:44.422 --> 00:07:46.664
You want me to do
my meanest look possible?


00:07:48.426 --> 00:07:51.294
- That might be a little extreme.
- Really? You go.


00:07:53.765 --> 00:07:56.257
Okay, we'll get you
out of that, then.


00:07:56.351 --> 00:07:57.351
Can I just...?


00:07:58.895 --> 00:08:00.978
All right, now you can take me out.


00:08:01.773 --> 00:08:03.480
So we get our cool jackets
done every year.


00:08:03.566 --> 00:08:06.309
This is for Season 7.
Adrian has one as well.


00:08:06.403 --> 00:08:09.191
A direwolf on the back,
"The North Remembers."


00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:12.569
"Stark" there on the arm. And then
the unit that you worked with.


00:08:12.659 --> 00:08:15.402
So Dragon, Wolf
and White Walker units.


00:08:15.495 --> 00:08:17.361
So Dragon out of Belfast.


00:08:18.373 --> 00:08:20.373
Whenever you see the season
starting back up again,


00:08:20.458 --> 00:08:23.917
you just see beards and these
black jackets walking around Belfast.


00:08:31.845 --> 00:08:33.285
What's that?


00:08:59.873 --> 00:09:02.160
I remember
reading the script.


00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:04.663
I remember being in Dubrovnik.


00:09:04.753 --> 00:09:07.496
And I remember saying to him, "We'll
never be allowed to shoot here,"


00:09:07.589 --> 00:09:09.251
just knowing what we had to do.


00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:11.753
Nobody was ever gonna let them
destroy their town,


00:09:11.843 --> 00:09:14.551
no matter where we were,
particularly not Dubrovnik.


00:09:14.637 --> 00:09:17.300
And then when we looked
outside of the production office,


00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:21.885
there's this great big,
flat piece of concreted land.


00:09:21.978 --> 00:09:23.970
You know, the Titanic Studios
need a backlot,


00:09:24.064 --> 00:09:27.023
and there was one really
obvious one sitting here.


00:09:29.819 --> 00:09:32.152
Phil and I are both
scratching out different ideas


00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:34.230
for our King's Landing street.


00:09:34.324 --> 00:09:39.410
We've been so many places and
photographed so many things that


00:09:39.496 --> 00:09:42.864
it's actually trying to work out
what makes these things fantastic.


00:09:42.957 --> 00:09:45.165
But it's gonna be a big build,
so we need to make sure


00:09:45.251 --> 00:09:48.289
it's worth the money and time
that'll be invested.


00:09:48.379 --> 00:09:50.871
And also, they're not sacrificing
going to a location


00:09:50.965 --> 00:09:54.458
to, instead, be shooting
in a really bad set.


00:09:55.136 --> 00:09:58.504
March 2013, when I first landed,


00:09:58.598 --> 00:10:02.217
it was so daunting,
but at the same time,


00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:04.142
we just couldn't let ourselves fail.


00:10:04.229 --> 00:10:05.686
I don't have it so much anymore,


00:10:05.772 --> 00:10:07.980
but I do certainly,
in the first year, remember having


00:10:08.066 --> 00:10:13.278
this constant tape in my head of,
"You are being employed to cope.


00:10:13.363 --> 00:10:15.400
Just cope, you just have to cope."


00:10:17.659 --> 00:10:20.117
But now I realize
all we were ever doing


00:10:20.203 --> 00:10:23.571
in Seasons 4, 5, 6 and 7
were training for Season 8.


00:10:43.017 --> 00:10:45.179
We did have a fence
all the way along here,


00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.933
but unfortunately the winds
knocked the fence down


00:10:48.022 --> 00:10:50.605
so we'll have to get
a whole new fence in.


00:10:50.692 --> 00:10:53.651
You don't wanna spoil it for people
because they'll see it.


00:10:53.736 --> 00:10:56.228
And then it'll spoil it for me
as well, like.


00:10:56.322 --> 00:10:58.564
- Do you watch the show?
- Oh, God, I love it.


00:11:00.535 --> 00:11:02.527
Oh, I wouldn't know.


00:11:03.496 --> 00:11:04.782
I know nothing.


00:11:06.791 --> 00:11:09.579
I'm really just looking for a part
in <i>Game of Thrones,</i>


00:11:09.669 --> 00:11:11.376
so put a word in for me,
that'd be great.


00:11:11.462 --> 00:11:14.876
One of the walking dead,
that'll do me.


00:11:14.966 --> 00:11:16.923
I've got the baldy head for it.


00:11:25.852 --> 00:11:27.684
When did the cast get scripts?


00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:29.206
They've had them three days.


00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:32.018
I don't know
who has just read their parts


00:11:32.108 --> 00:11:36.022
and who's read the full things, but
they've had a little time with them.


00:11:36.112 --> 00:11:40.823
For some of them, it might be
the first time they realize they die.


00:11:40.909 --> 00:11:42.741
I know Kit hasn't read his.


00:11:42.827 --> 00:11:46.946
Yeah, if they've not read them or...
We've given them to them.


00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:49.828
It's up to them if they wanna
read them before coming in.


00:12:00.595 --> 00:12:01.676
Soon, soon.


00:12:09.145 --> 00:12:10.477
Hey.


00:12:12.148 --> 00:12:13.389
Meaning, "Let's talk, come on."


00:12:25.995 --> 00:12:28.112
This is strange.


00:12:28.206 --> 00:12:31.040
We remember hoping against all hope


00:12:31.125 --> 00:12:33.833
that we would get
our first table read


00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:36.207
for the first season,
and here we are at the last one.


00:12:36.297 --> 00:12:37.788
And it really is...


00:12:37.882 --> 00:12:42.752
It's like looking around a table
and seeing your family, you know.


00:12:42.845 --> 00:12:44.990
- Except that we all get along.
- They're way better looking.


00:12:52.272 --> 00:12:53.666
"Exterior, Winterfell wall.


00:12:53.690 --> 00:12:55.272
The battle for Winterfell begins,


00:12:55.358 --> 00:12:58.442
heavily adapted, believe it or not,
for read through purposes.


00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:04.740
The Night King turns, sees Jon. Is
this going to be an epic fight? No.


00:13:04.826 --> 00:13:07.614
The Night King raises his arm slowly.


00:13:08.288 --> 00:13:09.574
Jon knows what that means.


00:13:09.664 --> 00:13:11.530
- The dead begin to rise.
- Shit.


00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:13.240
Jorah the Andal battles on.


00:13:13.334 --> 00:13:15.701
He has been slashed and stabbed,
pummeled and pierced,


00:13:15.795 --> 00:13:19.084
but somehow he keeps fighting.
Wights plunge their knives into him.


00:13:19.173 --> 00:13:21.460
He takes more punishment
than Hodor took at the door...


00:13:21.551 --> 00:13:23.153
- Aw.
- ...than Beric took in the Great Hall,


00:13:23.177 --> 00:13:26.045
and still somehow Jorah stands
and defends his queen.


00:13:26.139 --> 00:13:28.256
Dany tries to rouse Jorah,
but he is gone.


00:13:29.684 --> 00:13:30.764
Exterior, godswood.


00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:33.427
The Night King walks
with methodical, terrifying calm.


00:13:33.521 --> 00:13:36.013
He stops before Bran,
and raises his sword to strike,


00:13:36.107 --> 00:13:38.724
but something is hurtling toward him
out of the darkness. Arya.


00:13:41.362 --> 00:13:43.649
She vaults off a pile of dead wights,


00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:45.982
leaps at the Night King,
and she plunges the dagger


00:13:46.075 --> 00:13:48.783
up through the Night King's armor.
The Night King shatters.


00:13:56.002 --> 00:13:58.164
Wildlings and Northerners
have gathered around Jon.


00:13:58.254 --> 00:14:00.496
I saw him riding that thing.


00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:03.173
- We all did.
- No, no.


00:14:03.259 --> 00:14:07.629
I saw him riding that thing.


00:14:09.098 --> 00:14:11.260
That's right. You saw it.


00:14:11.351 --> 00:14:13.718
- I did.
- You did.


00:14:16.022 --> 00:14:18.810
That's why we all agreed
to follow him.


00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:20.607
Dragonstone Beach, night.


00:14:20.693 --> 00:14:23.106
Grey Worm leads Varys,
hands bound, down the beach.


00:14:23.196 --> 00:14:25.438
I told you what would happen
if you betrayed me.


00:14:25.531 --> 00:14:26.531
You did.


00:14:27.325 --> 00:14:28.941
Lord Varys,


00:14:29.035 --> 00:14:31.277
I, Daenerys of House Targaryen,


00:14:31.371 --> 00:14:33.738
First of My Name, Breaker of Chains


00:14:33.831 --> 00:14:36.289
and Mother of Dragons,
sentence you to die.


00:14:38.586 --> 00:14:40.873
<i>- Dracarys.</i>
- Drogon spews fire on him,


00:14:40.963 --> 00:14:42.670
but we don't watch
our old friend burn.


00:14:42.757 --> 00:14:45.249
Instead, we see the reactions
of those who knew him.


00:14:45.343 --> 00:14:47.960
Tyrion is heartbroken,
Jon is disturbed,


00:14:48.054 --> 00:14:51.138
Grey Worm sees this
as the just execution of a traitor.


00:14:51.224 --> 00:14:54.513
Did she sound
like someone who's done fighting?


00:14:54.602 --> 00:14:55.683
She's a conqueror.


00:14:56.354 --> 00:14:58.220
She liberated the people
of Slaver's Bay,


00:14:58.314 --> 00:15:00.431
she liberated the people
of King's Landing.


00:15:01.109 --> 00:15:03.567
Our queen's nature
is fire and blood.


00:15:03.653 --> 00:15:05.047
Standing before
the Iron Throne,


00:15:05.071 --> 00:15:07.028
Dany steps forward
and kisses the man she loves.


00:15:07.115 --> 00:15:09.027
A perfect kiss. Their eyes closed,


00:15:09.117 --> 00:15:11.655
his hand behind her head,
her hand on his cheek.


00:15:11.744 --> 00:15:15.579
Dany's eyes open suddenly
as she draws a sharp breath.


00:15:15.665 --> 00:15:18.453
Jon's eyes open as well,
already filling with tears.


00:15:18.543 --> 00:15:21.877
For a moment, neither moves,
as if moving will make this real.


00:15:21.963 --> 00:15:24.296
We see Jon with his hand
still on the hilt of the dagger


00:15:24.382 --> 00:15:27.216
he just lodged in Dany's heart.


00:15:31.013 --> 00:15:34.802
Her strength leaves her,
and she collapses to the marble.


00:15:34.892 --> 00:15:37.179
He keeps her in his arms,
and she falls.


00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.977
Kneeling down
to the floor beside her,


00:15:40.022 --> 00:15:43.106
he looks down at what he's done.
Terrible and necessary.


00:15:43.192 --> 00:15:45.229
End of <i>Game of Thrones."</i>


00:16:04.922 --> 00:16:06.288
So...


00:16:24.775 --> 00:16:26.437
Winter's coming, yeah.


00:16:27.487 --> 00:16:30.730
I am the snow man, okay?
Leave it with me.


00:16:31.824 --> 00:16:34.988
When they started on Season 1,
it was just one forest.


00:16:35.077 --> 00:16:37.410
And because this is the final season,


00:16:37.497 --> 00:16:42.413
then, yeah, everything seems to be
bigger, and heavier and more snow.


00:16:43.544 --> 00:16:46.912
It's just paper.
Paper and water, and it does the job.


00:16:53.971 --> 00:16:57.681
You probably need to go
into that hay doober, Steve.


00:16:57.767 --> 00:17:00.851
It's just trying to work out
where we need to put stuff


00:17:00.937 --> 00:17:02.303
and where we don't, you know?


00:17:02.396 --> 00:17:05.104
You can reckon
"Right, we're just seeing that,"


00:17:05.191 --> 00:17:07.399
but you move the camera just an inch,


00:17:07.485 --> 00:17:10.819
and it's another 10 meters
that you have to dress.


00:17:10.905 --> 00:17:12.771
You can't just throw money
at things, you know?


00:17:12.865 --> 00:17:13.981
I'm a stickler for that.


00:17:14.075 --> 00:17:15.691
I don't like to give away
too much money.


00:17:15.785 --> 00:17:17.026
I don't like to waste anything.


00:17:17.119 --> 00:17:20.203
I know it's not mine,
but don't waste it, you know?


00:17:20.289 --> 00:17:21.725
What are you gonna do
if it snows?


00:17:21.749 --> 00:17:24.583
If it snows?
Oh, I'll probably have a party.


00:17:24.669 --> 00:17:26.706
If it snows, yeah,
cover the whole lot in white.


00:17:26.796 --> 00:17:29.960
That would be fantastic. But
it's just not gonna happen, is it?


00:17:30.049 --> 00:17:32.757
It just rains in Belfast.


00:17:35.346 --> 00:17:37.824
<i>- Must be Naomi.</i>
- If that's horse feed,


00:17:37.848 --> 00:17:40.807
it needs to come up to me
at the horse marquee.


00:17:40.893 --> 00:17:42.885
<i>They're fucking lying everywhere.</i>


00:17:42.979 --> 00:17:45.471
What the fuck
are you talking about?


00:17:45.565 --> 00:17:47.807
<i>They've been threw off
and they're lying everywhere.</i>


00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.141
They came on a tipper


00:17:49.235 --> 00:17:52.649
so we just have to fucking tip them
into the fucking grass.


00:17:52.738 --> 00:17:54.274
<i>Hey, man, don't worry.</i>


00:17:56.158 --> 00:17:58.616
So I'm the location manager.


00:17:58.703 --> 00:18:01.366
You can have 350 crew,


00:18:01.455 --> 00:18:05.665
and with that comes
the infrastructure,


00:18:05.751 --> 00:18:10.166
service vehicles, extras, marquees.


00:18:10.256 --> 00:18:13.249
I sort of end up
doing all the logistics


00:18:13.342 --> 00:18:15.880
and the running of all the locations


