When I first came on board,
Chris sent me a picture of Iceland.


00:52:23.015 --> 00:52:25.632
I saw that picture and I said,
"Yeah, that's what we need."


00:52:26.852 --> 00:52:29.845
And I pitched it to HBO.


00:52:29.938 --> 00:52:33.522
So little was known about
how short the days were,


00:52:33.609 --> 00:52:35.271
how risky it was.


00:52:35.361 --> 00:52:36.818
Nobody questioned it.


00:52:39.615 --> 00:52:41.777
It's such a magical place.


00:52:41.867 --> 00:52:46.737
When that sun rises, it's like
somebody slowly unwrapping a present.


00:52:47.581 --> 00:52:48.913
Good morning.


00:52:48.999 --> 00:52:50.490
How are the bones?


00:52:54.588 --> 00:52:56.204
Start walking around.


00:52:58.133 --> 00:52:59.169
All right.


00:53:06.475 --> 00:53:08.137
I don't know
how to ride a dragon.


00:53:08.227 --> 00:53:09.468
Nobody does.


00:53:09.561 --> 00:53:11.302
Until they ride a dragon.


00:53:11.397 --> 00:53:13.764
Nose. No, get in.


00:53:13.857 --> 00:53:15.393
Get in for the nose.


00:53:16.860 --> 00:53:19.978
I could do with this amount of snow
around me all the time.


00:53:20.072 --> 00:53:21.654
If we were in boats.


00:53:21.740 --> 00:53:23.572
- Seriously.
- Everybody back, please.


00:53:23.659 --> 00:53:25.821
Guys, let's clear the eye lines.
Goodbye.


00:53:25.911 --> 00:53:27.389
- Thank you.
- I'm the only one


00:53:27.413 --> 00:53:29.826
that's allowed to shout around here.


00:53:29.915 --> 00:53:32.578
It's not looking quite as tidy
as it once did.


00:53:33.502 --> 00:53:34.709
She's split.


00:53:36.797 --> 00:53:39.164
Bloody hair's just moved again.


00:53:41.719 --> 00:53:43.599
Do you have an opinion
on our hand warmers?


00:53:43.637 --> 00:53:45.253
Pan left, pan out.


00:53:45.347 --> 00:53:46.758
Snow.


00:53:47.891 --> 00:53:49.473
- Snow.
- Snow.


00:53:49.560 --> 00:53:51.176
Jon Snow in snow.


00:53:53.480 --> 00:53:56.894
Ready, and action.


00:53:56.984 --> 00:53:58.941
Move to your right
a little bit, Emilia.


00:53:59.027 --> 00:54:00.859
And growl.


00:54:00.946 --> 00:54:03.859
One more kiss, a little more,
and Emilia go a little to your right.


00:54:03.949 --> 00:54:07.818
Kissing and moving around, and still.


00:54:07.911 --> 00:54:08.911
Growl.


00:54:09.913 --> 00:54:12.530
One more, ready? Growl.


00:54:13.375 --> 00:54:15.241
He kept right, got it.
Check the gate.


00:54:15.335 --> 00:54:16.542
Moving on.


00:54:17.880 --> 00:54:20.608
I think in our hearts,
it was important for us to come here.


00:54:20.632 --> 00:54:22.715
It wouldn't have felt the same
if we didn't.


00:54:24.052 --> 00:54:26.669
It just makes my heart really smile.


00:54:38.567 --> 00:54:40.024
<i>Nine minutes to 7.</i>


00:54:40.110 --> 00:54:42.978
<i>The so-called "beast from the east"
is making its presence felt</i>


00:54:43.071 --> 00:54:44.903
<i>in both Britain and Ireland.</i>


00:54:44.990 --> 00:54:47.051
<i>Ireland under
the highest weather warning,</i>


00:54:47.075 --> 00:54:49.863
<i>with the worst snow seen
for 35 years.</i>


00:54:49.953 --> 00:54:52.515
<i>Four hundred and forty
schools will be closed today.</i>


00:54:52.539 --> 00:54:54.280
<i>People have been told
to stay indoors.</i>


00:55:13.352 --> 00:55:14.843
I need to get back here by 10.


00:55:14.937 --> 00:55:17.850
That's all because
we can't open the doors anymore.


00:55:17.940 --> 00:55:19.181
- What?
- We should...


00:55:19.274 --> 00:55:22.563
In usual circumstances,
we would just take that straight out.


00:55:27.199 --> 00:55:30.317
We're so, so tight now
in terms of time


00:55:30.410 --> 00:55:34.996
that something like, you know,
this sort of poor weather


00:55:35.082 --> 00:55:37.449
makes this a much bigger deal for us
than it should.


00:55:37.543 --> 00:55:39.455
Is this a harder season
than others?


00:55:39.545 --> 00:55:42.162
- By a long, long way.
- By a long shot, yeah.


00:55:42.256 --> 00:55:44.088
The schedule is impossible.
Um...


00:55:46.426 --> 00:55:47.883
The season is very big.


00:55:47.970 --> 00:55:50.883
It's written very big, but we have...


00:55:50.973 --> 00:55:53.966
It's just all this business
of trying to do,


00:55:54.059 --> 00:55:57.848
you know, film finishes on
a TV schedule and on a TV deadline...


00:55:58.814 --> 00:55:59.850
And I think this season,


00:56:00.023 --> 00:56:01.389
we've certainly found the limit


00:56:01.483 --> 00:56:03.019
of what's able to be achieved.


00:56:03.110 --> 00:56:06.319
And insofar as I think


00:56:06.405 --> 00:56:10.240
now everybody realizes
that <i>Game of Thrones</i> has to finish


00:56:10.325 --> 00:56:13.284
because it just cannot get any bigger.


00:56:13.370 --> 00:56:15.953
You know, there are a lot of
frayed nerves walking around,


00:56:16.039 --> 00:56:17.405
myself being one of them.


00:56:27.634 --> 00:56:32.174
We're still totally
100 percent frozen over at tomb.


00:56:32.264 --> 00:56:35.928
I mean, yesterday, we had 250 extras


00:56:36.018 --> 00:56:39.136
and all the crew, and not one toilet.


00:56:39.229 --> 00:56:42.472
In the bowls, the bleach was frozen.


00:56:42.566 --> 00:56:45.183
<i>- That's wild.</i>
- Oh, it was the icicles


00:56:45.277 --> 00:56:48.270
hanging off the taps
that I couldn't believe.


00:56:48.363 --> 00:56:50.696
You try and preempt
as much as you can,


00:56:50.782 --> 00:56:54.492
but sometimes it just gets to a stage


00:56:54.578 --> 00:56:59.744
where, you know, you just can't
hold Mother Nature back anymore.


00:57:04.463 --> 00:57:08.082
I mean, it's starting to
snow again now, so it's one of them.


00:57:08.175 --> 00:57:09.882
I can't say that
we're gonna do any work


00:57:09.968 --> 00:57:12.335
until I know that we can do some work.


00:57:12.429 --> 00:57:14.637
Is that a good enough answer for you?


00:57:16.099 --> 00:57:18.466
I can't really say anything else
because it's snowing.


00:57:18.560 --> 00:57:22.304
And if it snows, well, we can't just
dress on top of real snow.


00:57:22.397 --> 00:57:25.561
Cheers. Thanks a lot. Bye. Bye.


00:57:30.155 --> 00:57:33.319
It was not a good idea
to be doing it in the winter.


00:57:33.408 --> 00:57:36.321
You needed to have spread
the snow locations out


00:57:36.411 --> 00:57:39.495
because we can't do that many
at one time.


00:57:39.581 --> 00:57:41.538
Look at all this nonsense,


00:57:41.625 --> 00:57:43.227
it just keeps coming
through all the time.


00:57:43.251 --> 00:57:44.458
And it's like, "Right, okay.


00:57:44.544 --> 00:57:47.912
Like I've got time to keep pulling
my phone out of my pocket."


00:57:48.632 --> 00:57:53.218
Through zigzag roads, they made us
put up a horizon the night before,


00:57:53.303 --> 00:57:55.386
came in in the morning ready to shoot:


00:57:55.472 --> 00:57:59.341
"Can you take that down?"
So that's half a day of mine wasted.


00:58:02.062 --> 00:58:04.429
So, what we're doing
is getting this snow up


00:58:04.523 --> 00:58:07.812
so we can take it up to
Magheramorne, the battlefield.


00:58:07.901 --> 00:58:09.563
You know, we're just under the cosh.


00:58:11.238 --> 00:58:12.649
Ah, shit.


00:58:12.739 --> 00:58:14.526
The wind's blowing a good 'un here.


00:58:14.616 --> 00:58:17.859
Yeah, Dickie, you up at Magheramorne?


00:58:17.953 --> 00:58:19.910
Well, there's no water at all.


00:58:19.997 --> 00:58:22.785
Nightmare. All right, mate.
Ta-ra, ta-ra.


00:58:25.168 --> 00:58:27.330
It's all frozen up at Magheramorne.


00:58:27.421 --> 00:58:31.665
Now I have to sort out a pump
and pump it out the lake and... Argh!


00:58:32.551 --> 00:58:35.043
Fucking hell.


00:58:35.137 --> 00:58:37.629
- You okay, Del?
- It is all going.


00:58:37.723 --> 00:58:39.339
I just feel like crying.


00:58:43.395 --> 00:58:44.886
This car's got no bollocks.


00:58:44.980 --> 00:58:47.347
This Fiesta, stupid little thing.


00:58:52.738 --> 00:58:55.481
You know, it's difficult to find
people who know the job.


00:58:55.574 --> 00:58:56.815
It's not rocket science.


00:58:56.908 --> 00:58:58.820
I mean, you could do it, Jeanie.
It ain't hard.


00:59:03.206 --> 00:59:05.323
Welcome to hell, George.
Welcome to hell.


00:59:13.550 --> 00:59:15.883
I'm not one for listening
to people whinge.


00:59:15.969 --> 00:59:17.585
Oh, come on.


00:59:18.180 --> 00:59:21.014
I was brought up
in children's homes, you know.


00:59:21.099 --> 00:59:23.011
Didn't have a clue
where me mom and dad was.


00:59:23.101 --> 00:59:25.514
I left the homes
when I was 16 and a half.


00:59:25.604 --> 00:59:28.688
They give you 300 quid,
your bloody birth certificate.


00:59:28.774 --> 00:59:30.857
And, "Right.
Get yourself out there, then."


00:59:30.942 --> 00:59:34.026
It's like, "Hmm. Okay, then."
So, yeah, that opened my eyes.


00:59:35.489 --> 00:59:36.591
As I've progressed, you know,


00:59:36.615 --> 00:59:38.322
I've always got more money,
and I think:


00:59:38.408 --> 00:59:41.947
"To keep that, I just have to keep
working at the pace I'm working at."


00:59:42.037 --> 00:59:44.780
You just wanna do
the best for your kids.


00:59:44.873 --> 00:59:46.830
You know,
I'd give up my house for my kids.


01:00:00.764 --> 01:00:03.177
I've never
not done a set yet,


01:00:03.266 --> 01:00:05.178
but it's been very close twice.


01:00:05.268 --> 01:00:07.635
This is the second time
it's been close...


01:00:08.605 --> 01:00:11.894
But we'll get there, I think.


01:00:15.737 --> 01:00:16.737
Hi.


01:00:16.822 --> 01:00:18.582
My horses are dyed pink.


01:00:19.658 --> 01:00:21.650
- Don't even go there.
- Okay.


01:00:21.743 --> 01:00:24.326
They've tried warm water,
Fairy liquid.


01:00:24.412 --> 01:00:27.450
- I can't get them back to white.
- Look at the state of him.


01:00:27.541 --> 01:00:29.282
I know.
One of them looked like he's saying:


01:00:29.376 --> 01:00:31.618
"I'm pink. I don't like being pink."


01:00:35.298 --> 01:00:38.111
Magheramorne Quarry's been the
scene of the Battle of the Blackwater,


01:00:38.135 --> 01:00:41.048
Hardhome, it's also Castle Black.


01:00:41.138 --> 01:00:44.176
This is the biggest green screen
that I have ever seen,


01:00:44.266 --> 01:00:47.100
but it's really impressive
what they've built here.


01:00:52.065 --> 01:00:54.227
This battle sequence, I think,
we have coming up,


01:00:54.317 --> 01:00:57.651
they don't tend to tell us
a lot of stuff.


01:00:59.364 --> 01:01:00.900
On the day, one of the ADs


01:01:00.991 --> 01:01:04.075
get up and actually tell us
what's happening that day.


01:01:05.787 --> 01:01:07.779
The numbers we've just heard


01:01:07.873 --> 01:01:11.116
are 120,000 wights


01:01:11.209 --> 01:01:15.624
against 18,000 combined,


01:01:15.714 --> 01:01:19.754
in Daenerys's army
and Jon Snow's army as well, like.


01:01:19.843 --> 01:01:22.677
So we're extremely outnumbered.


01:01:23.555 --> 01:01:26.889
I can't even begin to imagine
how this is gonna look on TV.


01:01:33.023 --> 01:01:35.891
The way I like to think of it
is that the Extras Department


01:01:35.984 --> 01:01:39.398
is like one of the main actors.
Just as important.


01:01:40.697 --> 01:01:42.563
I got a close-up
at the Battle of the Bastards.


01:01:42.657 --> 01:01:44.865
I had no idea the camera was on me.


01:01:47.204 --> 01:01:51.198
Camera set.
And three, two, one...


01:01:52.584 --> 01:01:55.229
There's this collective thing
that we have that we're all in,


01:01:55.253 --> 01:01:58.496
trying to make this really,
really, really exciting, like.


01:01:58.590 --> 01:02:01.253
Because even the background
tells a big story.


01:02:02.302 --> 01:02:04.715
<i>Great stuff, thank you.
We have cut.</i>


01:02:05.555 --> 01:02:07.842
March! Left, right, left.


01:02:12.354 --> 01:02:14.937
- Don't penny up, darling.
- Cheers. Thank you very much.


01:02:17.776 --> 01:02:18.776
And a wee egg, sure.


01:02:18.860 --> 01:02:20.647
- Sophie, isn't it?
- Yeah, Sophie, yeah.


01:02:20.737 --> 01:02:22.194
- Nice to meet you.
- Huh?


01:02:22.280 --> 01:02:23.758
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you, too.


01:02:23.782 --> 01:02:26.616
Sophie Ellis-Bextor.
Couldn't believe it when she come up.


01:02:26.701 --> 01:02:29.785
I'm totally starstruck.
One of my favorites from years ago.


01:02:29.871 --> 01:02:33.114
You never get to see these people
any other time, you know?


01:02:33.208 --> 01:02:34.915
But, yeah.
It's like a wee dream sometimes.


01:02:35.001 --> 01:02:37.789
- And they're coming to you.
- I know. I know.


01:02:37.879 --> 01:02:40.041
And then she said I was well-stocked,
and I was like:


01:02:41.758 --> 01:02:43.249
Bonus.


01:02:44.761 --> 01:02:49.096
Very busy and a bit stressful
because of the nights.


01:02:49.182 --> 01:02:51.799
How many nights have we done so far?
14 weeks, 15 weeks, is it?


01:02:51.893 --> 01:02:54.226
No, we're on our ninth.


01:02:54.312 --> 01:02:55.519
- What?
- Yeah.


01:02:56.189 --> 01:02:58.226
Ninth. Yeah, it's only Week 9.


01:02:58.316 --> 01:03:00.683
It's only Week 9. Is it really?


01:03:00.777 --> 01:03:03.394
No, it's more than that.
We started in January.


01:03:09.452 --> 01:03:11.990
Is this the longest in run
of nights on <i>Game of Thrones?</i>


01:03:12.080 --> 01:03:13.742
Yes.


01:03:13.832 --> 01:03:15.824
In fact, we were
trying to think is this


01:03:15.917 --> 01:03:19.786
the longest time any film
has filmed nights?


01:03:20.880 --> 01:03:22.371
I guess I could try to Google that.


01:03:22.465 --> 01:03:25.924
What's the longest nights
of any film crew?


01:03:26.011 --> 01:03:27.171
A smoke nightmare.


01:03:28.138 --> 01:03:30.755
That's like smoke apocalypse.


01:03:30.849 --> 01:03:32.590
It's almost like a bad dream.


01:03:32.684 --> 01:03:37.270
I got to sleep at 9:30 in the morning
and I slept till 1:30.


01:03:37.355 --> 01:03:39.392
Three hours? Is that four hours?
I don't know.


01:03:39.482 --> 01:03:41.849
One of my best-ever anxiety dreams:


01:03:41.943 --> 01:03:45.778
It was a beautiful blue sky,
and there was a rope


01:03:45.864 --> 01:03:49.483
strung across my vision, and it
just got pulled taut, taut, taut,


01:03:49.576 --> 01:03:52.364
and then it snapped and I woke up.


01:03:53.580 --> 01:03:56.163
I don't fucking know.
It sounds like anxiety to me.


01:03:57.083 --> 01:03:59.020
<i>All right.
Background and stunts,</i>


01:03:59.044 --> 01:04:02.958
<i>until the moment we yell "cut,"
you need to hold your breath,</i>


01:04:03.048 --> 01:04:05.586
<i>but also not breathe out.</i>


01:04:05.675 --> 01:04:06.882
<i>It's gonna be amazing.</i>


01:04:06.968 --> 01:04:09.130
<i>If anybody dies, let me know.</i>


01:04:12.015 --> 01:04:13.815
- How you doing? How you feeling?
- Good time.


01:04:13.850 --> 01:04:16.763
Yeah?
Were you a little sore this morning?


01:04:16.853 --> 01:04:18.685
A little sore. Couple muscles ached.
Yeah.


01:04:18.772 --> 01:04:21.264
It just gets old,
these nights. Yes, sir.


01:04:22.233 --> 01:04:24.065
Uh, so, this...


01:04:24.152 --> 01:04:26.269
In this, you're dead.


01:04:26.363 --> 01:04:27.570
Dead.


01:04:27.655 --> 01:04:28.691
He dies?


01:04:30.283 --> 01:04:31.802
- The ending makes sense.
- Yes.


01:04:31.826 --> 01:04:33.158
Everything that's gone before.


01:04:33.244 --> 01:04:35.361
Certainly, the way
they're shooting it.


01:04:35.455 --> 01:04:37.071
That he'd die for her.


01:04:37.165 --> 01:04:39.498
Know what I mean?
It's a big part of her demise.


01:04:39.584 --> 01:04:40.950
Yes.


01:04:41.836 --> 01:04:44.544
<i>Ready, and action.</i>


01:05:26.464 --> 01:05:27.500
<i>Cut.</i>


01:05:33.430 --> 01:05:35.638
Good for A, mark out.


01:05:49.362 --> 01:05:53.231
Well, I can feel
the weariness setting in.


01:05:53.324 --> 01:05:57.409
Like tonight, Candi said,
"Oh, only 14 weeks till we wrap."


01:05:57.495 --> 01:06:01.284
And that made it sound like,
"What? No."


01:06:03.626 --> 01:06:06.585
It's a mixed thing.
One way you're wishing it away,


01:06:06.671 --> 01:06:10.005
like, "Oh, please, let's just get
through this, this and this."


01:06:10.967 --> 01:06:14.335
And then the other one is like,
"No, I don't want this to end."


01:06:31.029 --> 01:06:33.112
This is a godswood tree.


01:06:33.198 --> 01:06:35.235
I think it's a magical sort of tree.


01:06:35.325 --> 01:06:39.194
It goes back, way back in time.
And Children of the Forest...


01:06:39.287 --> 01:06:42.906
To do the Children of the Forest,
they'll be facing the front of it.


01:06:43.249 --> 01:06:48.085
Um, but I don't really... To be honest,
I don't really know. You know, but...


01:06:48.171 --> 01:06:49.878
Have you done
the godswood before?


01:06:49.964 --> 01:06:53.378
I do it every year.
My seventh year now.


01:06:53.468 --> 01:06:55.710
Have you got
a favorite character?


01:06:55.803 --> 01:06:59.513
I did like Stannis before he killed
his daughter, like, you know.


01:06:59.599 --> 01:07:01.636
And I like, at the minute...


01:07:02.602 --> 01:07:05.310
I actually like the Night King,
you know?


01:07:06.314 --> 01:07:07.833
You know
what's gonna happen to him?


01:07:07.857 --> 01:07:09.849
Yeah, I do. I do.


01:07:11.152 --> 01:07:12.188
Yeah.


01:07:16.074 --> 01:07:18.111
When I read this,
it's up to me,


01:07:18.201 --> 01:07:20.944
maybe it will be good
when Bran will kill me.


01:07:21.037 --> 01:07:23.996
So Arya, she will appear,
I will grab her or something,


01:07:24.082 --> 01:07:27.826
then maybe I will kill Arya,
and Bran, he kill me.


01:07:27.919 --> 01:07:30.457
- He will throw the knife to me.
- Just throw it.


01:07:30.547 --> 01:07:34.791
And then this make Night King angry,
you know?


01:07:34.884 --> 01:07:38.048
I am happy,
and then, okay, he looking at me,


01:07:38.137 --> 01:07:42.051
and then I see on his eyes
and body like:


01:07:42.141 --> 01:07:45.134
"Oh, mmm, Night King."


01:07:45.228 --> 01:07:46.309
And then I...


01:07:46.396 --> 01:07:48.353
Mmm... Okay.


01:07:50.108 --> 01:07:52.020
Arya will kill me.


01:07:52.110 --> 01:07:55.444
The girl kill Night King,
how is this possible?


01:07:58.157 --> 01:08:00.774
This year I don't feel
so very comfortable


01:08:00.868 --> 01:08:03.326
because I don't know where I belong.


01:08:04.664 --> 01:08:08.999
If I'm part of the actor
or I'm part of the stuntmen.


01:08:10.253 --> 01:08:11.289
<i>Action.</i>


01:08:11.379 --> 01:08:13.917
Many times the stunts
are joking with me:


01:08:14.007 --> 01:08:16.841
"Hey, you're the Night King,
you don't need to do nothing."


01:08:17.594 --> 01:08:20.837
Sometimes I thinking,
"No, is that true?"


01:08:20.930 --> 01:08:24.173
When we finish Night King stuff,
I can do some fire job,


01:08:24.267 --> 01:08:27.886
and falling from the stairs
or some fight.


01:08:27.979 --> 01:08:29.095
I looking forward.


01:08:30.773 --> 01:08:32.730
- Yeah, I like that. I like that.
- That's good?


01:08:32.817 --> 01:08:35.901
- That's good.
- So cast can step off. Thank you.


01:08:41.284 --> 01:08:43.071
They called you
a bit early, Vlad.


01:08:44.245 --> 01:08:46.953
- Classic.
- It's the movie business.


01:08:47.040 --> 01:08:48.076
Yeah.


01:08:48.791 --> 01:08:52.535
- Waiting, one hour, two hours.
- Hurry up and wait, yep.


01:08:52.629 --> 01:08:54.712
Do something. Okay. And then again,


01:08:54.797 --> 01:08:56.288
- wait, wait.
- Yeah.


01:08:57.216 --> 01:08:58.798
- Yep.
- Kill him, kill him.


01:08:58.885 --> 01:09:00.885
- Yeah, kill him. Yeah.
- And then wait.


01:09:08.603 --> 01:09:09.969
<i>And camera.</i>


01:09:10.063 --> 01:09:13.727
<i>Three, two, one, action!</i>


01:09:32.877 --> 01:09:36.917
Instead of it being a death
like that, it's just a...


01:09:37.006 --> 01:09:39.464
Before you even get to be surprised.


01:09:40.760 --> 01:09:41.796
Got it.


01:09:43.513 --> 01:09:45.991
Could you... Let's just
practice dropping that knife.


01:09:46.015 --> 01:09:48.177
Ready. Yeah. Okay, that's good.


01:09:48.267 --> 01:09:49.678
That really helps.


01:09:49.769 --> 01:09:51.305
You should be on him all the time.


01:09:51.396 --> 01:09:52.477
Yep.


01:09:53.398 --> 01:09:56.266
Miguel, he showed me the way.


01:09:56.359 --> 01:09:58.351
Move from A to B.


01:09:58.444 --> 01:10:00.436
It looks like easy...


01:10:01.989 --> 01:10:04.481
but it's definitely not so easy.


01:10:04.575 --> 01:10:08.364
So I... Sometimes I realize be actor
is not easy to be.


01:10:08.454 --> 01:10:09.932
It's better to be stuntman.


01:10:09.956 --> 01:10:13.245
<i>Set.
Three, two, one, action!</i>


01:10:14.377 --> 01:10:15.834
<i>Stab him. Good.</i>


01:10:15.920 --> 01:10:17.001
<i>Action.</i>


01:10:18.005 --> 01:10:19.041
<i>Stab him.</i>


01:10:22.051 --> 01:10:24.196
- Rolling reset, thank you.
- Still rolling!


01:10:24.220 --> 01:10:25.461
Back to ones.


01:10:29.726 --> 01:10:30.726
Ready?


01:10:30.810 --> 01:10:31.810
<i>And...</i>


01:10:31.894 --> 01:10:35.478
Three, two, one, action!


01:10:35.565 --> 01:10:36.601
Drop!


01:10:37.775 --> 01:10:39.186
<i>And now turn.</i>


01:10:39.277 --> 01:10:40.609
<i>Look up.</i>


01:10:40.695 --> 01:10:42.277
<i>Down. Stab him.</i>


01:10:42.905 --> 01:10:43.905
One more.


01:10:43.990 --> 01:10:46.403
<i>Action! Action!</i>


01:10:46.492 --> 01:10:49.075
<i>Three, two, one, action!</i>


01:10:52.457 --> 01:10:53.993
<i>Now cut. Well done.</i>


01:11:22.695 --> 01:11:24.231
We've been doing night shoots.


01:11:24.322 --> 01:11:26.314
I can't remember what week this is.


01:11:26.407 --> 01:11:29.821
You sort of wake up,
quickly get showered,


01:11:29.911 --> 01:11:33.905
drive to location, shoot all day,
get back on the minibus,


01:11:33.998 --> 01:11:36.331
quickly try and get some sleep,
wake up.


01:11:36.417 --> 01:11:38.659
It is like <i>Groundhog Day.</i>


01:11:38.753 --> 01:11:41.541
When anybody ever says,
"How's it going, Sarah?"


01:11:41.631 --> 01:11:43.122
I feel like saying:


01:11:44.926 --> 01:11:46.508
"I'm broken."


01:11:47.762 --> 01:11:50.550
We feel like vampires, don't we?
I mean, seriously.


01:11:50.640 --> 01:11:52.848
It's like everybody's just gray,
aren't they?


01:11:52.934 --> 01:11:56.018
<i>Just roll it
through once so I can see it.</i>


01:11:56.103 --> 01:11:58.186
Unit call was at 8 p.m.


01:11:58.272 --> 01:12:01.310
They're supposed to wrap at 6 a.m.


01:12:01.400 --> 01:12:02.732
We don't ever wrap early.


01:12:02.819 --> 01:12:06.859
But there's a rumor going around
that we might wrap at 3.


01:12:07.907 --> 01:12:10.775
When people start rumors
like that, it's, uh...


01:12:12.995 --> 01:12:13.995
It can only get...


01:12:14.080 --> 01:12:16.242
It's disappointing
if we're still here at 6.


01:12:17.333 --> 01:12:19.666
When does Lottie get here
to be an extra?


01:12:19.752 --> 01:12:21.709
My mother flew her over


01:12:21.796 --> 01:12:24.379
so we can watch Lottie
being filmed for the day.


01:12:24.465 --> 01:12:26.252
I haven't seen her for three weeks.


01:12:26.342 --> 01:12:28.425
Then there's all the snow.


01:12:28.511 --> 01:12:30.844
I've really struggled
this shoot, actually.


01:12:32.557 --> 01:12:33.798
It's hard.


01:12:33.891 --> 01:12:35.257
It's hard being a mum.


01:12:36.352 --> 01:12:38.560
You know, I missed her Mother's Day...


01:12:39.897 --> 01:12:42.765
um, assembly.


01:12:42.859 --> 01:12:45.021
And I missed her Easter bonnet parade.


01:12:47.154 --> 01:12:48.895
In the grand scheme of things,
it's not...


01:12:48.990 --> 01:12:51.277
You know,
you say it's not that long...


01:12:52.201 --> 01:12:57.117
but when you're living each day,
it is a long time.


01:12:58.207 --> 01:13:00.620
I need checks on Walkers,
thank you.


01:13:03.880 --> 01:13:05.667
We're rolling away.


01:13:05.756 --> 01:13:07.122
And action.


01:13:11.387 --> 01:13:14.050
- Cut. Got it, lovely.
- That's a cut.


01:13:14.140 --> 01:13:17.133
<i>- That is a wrap, good night.</i>
- That's a wrap!


01:13:18.728 --> 01:13:19.764
It's a wrap!


01:13:20.938 --> 01:13:22.304
I hope. It's a wrap.


01:13:22.398 --> 01:13:24.606
<i>Guys, thanks very much
for the last few months.</i>


01:13:24.692 --> 01:13:25.692
Aw.


01:13:25.776 --> 01:13:27.233
<i>Have an excellent Easter.</i>


01:13:27.320 --> 01:13:30.484
<i>Enjoy yourselves, get some rest,
party hard, come back fresh.</i>


01:13:35.036 --> 01:13:36.805
Do you know what
you're going to do today?


01:13:36.829 --> 01:13:40.869
I think I might go and film
at the Belfast...


01:13:40.958 --> 01:13:42.950
The Belfast...


01:13:43.044 --> 01:13:44.501
<i>Game of Thrones</i> show.


01:13:46.172 --> 01:13:47.208
Hi.


01:14:02.855 --> 01:14:05.313
I love your beautiful hair clip.


01:14:13.658 --> 01:14:15.194
- Who is it?
- The Night King.


01:14:15.284 --> 01:14:17.321
- And who else?
- And Jon Snow.


01:14:22.124 --> 01:14:23.124
Lottie.


01:14:23.209 --> 01:14:24.825
- That's a very exotic name.
- Yeah.


01:14:38.474 --> 01:14:40.807
She's, like, dragging it.


01:15:48.502 --> 01:15:50.118
Is this Roman, then, this thing?


01:15:51.213 --> 01:15:53.205
Throw him to the lions,
that sort of thing?


01:15:53.299 --> 01:15:54.943
You weren't here
on a previous shoot?


01:15:54.967 --> 01:15:57.254
No, no. This is the first time for me.


01:15:57.344 --> 01:16:00.803
Every year before,
"No, I'm not going to Spain. No."


01:16:00.890 --> 01:16:02.973
But there was never anything to do.


01:16:04.518 --> 01:16:06.180
Only supposed to be around the outside


01:16:06.270 --> 01:16:08.478
where the Unsullied are,
you know, but...


01:16:12.193 --> 01:16:13.795
Yeah, I don't know
what I'm doing here.


01:16:13.819 --> 01:16:17.153
You boys could have done it
in your spare time.


01:16:20.326 --> 01:16:22.909
Don't Debbie dozy.
There we are, Jeanie, that's it.


01:16:22.995 --> 01:16:24.907
I don't think it's even worth
doing the machine.


01:16:24.997 --> 01:16:28.206
We may as well just run it
out of the bags.


01:16:31.962 --> 01:16:34.579
In Season 7,
Jaime was in King's Landing


01:16:34.673 --> 01:16:37.165
and a snowflake landed on his hand,
didn't it?


01:16:37.259 --> 01:16:41.253
So that allows you then
to put little bits wherever.


01:16:41.347 --> 01:16:45.717
There isn't going to be much snow
apparently, so it's just me.


01:16:51.982 --> 01:16:55.066
Not too much,
just to say that it's blown in...


01:16:56.112 --> 01:16:57.273
and stayed.


01:17:01.826 --> 01:17:04.534
Yep, that does it for me.


01:17:06.539 --> 01:17:09.907
It's award-winning snow, Del.
Does that mean anything?


01:17:10.000 --> 01:17:11.000
Yeah, it's great.


01:17:11.085 --> 01:17:12.826
They brought the Emmys out to the set


01:17:12.920 --> 01:17:15.253
so everybody could have
their photograph taken with them.


01:17:15.339 --> 01:17:18.923
It's the first time I've ever had
my photograph taken with the Emmy.


01:17:19.009 --> 01:17:21.877
Not that I'd show anything,
"Oh, this is my Emmy."


01:17:21.971 --> 01:17:24.759
I've got a certificate.
We got the, you know, original...


01:17:24.849 --> 01:17:28.388
We had to pay for it, but, you know,
I don't mind paying for it.


01:17:28.477 --> 01:17:32.346
You know, so, yeah. I was part of
the Emmy award-winning...


01:17:32.439 --> 01:17:33.439
So, yeah.


01:17:33.524 --> 01:17:34.890
But you don't show that, do you?


01:17:34.984 --> 01:17:37.101
It's like having a forklift license.


01:17:50.624 --> 01:17:53.458
It's very hard to keep
the cast quiet because when in Spain,


01:17:53.544 --> 01:17:55.877
you must eat and drink,
so they're gonna be out and about.


01:17:55.963 --> 01:17:59.001
And so we brought in a few ringers.


01:17:59.091 --> 01:18:00.457
We have the Waif coming in


01:18:00.551 --> 01:18:05.262
because so many people think that
Arya is dead and the Waif killed her.


01:18:05.347 --> 01:18:09.808
We have Jaqen, who's also another
House of Black and White character.


01:18:13.439 --> 01:18:14.850
And we have the Night King here.


01:18:14.940 --> 01:18:17.683
Not quite sure
what he would be saying.


01:18:17.776 --> 01:18:20.985
So they won't know what's happening.


01:18:21.071 --> 01:18:23.028
It'll be a big surprise,
no matter what.


01:18:28.913 --> 01:18:30.404
Jon Snow is here!


01:18:34.168 --> 01:18:35.750
You are not here to speak.


01:18:35.836 --> 01:18:40.456
I've had nothing to do
but think these past few weeks.


01:18:42.176 --> 01:18:44.714
About our bloody history.


01:18:44.803 --> 01:18:49.389
There's nothing in the world
more powerful than a good story.


01:18:49.475 --> 01:18:53.810
And who has a better story
than Bran the Broken?


01:19:01.362 --> 01:19:05.106
It's weird,
I've come out basically as decoy.


01:19:05.199 --> 01:19:08.363
It feels weird being here
and not actually filming.


01:19:10.162 --> 01:19:14.497
When all the Spanish fans shout
"Kit," they shout, "Keet, Keet!"


01:19:14.583 --> 01:19:18.042
So the rest of the cast
have now dubbed me Keet.


01:19:18.128 --> 01:19:20.745
- Keet!
- Keet! Keet!


01:19:22.007 --> 01:19:26.718
- Please. Keet!
- Please, please, please.


01:19:26.804 --> 01:19:28.340
Hi. Hi, hello.


01:19:32.685 --> 01:19:34.347
Keet!


01:19:34.436 --> 01:19:35.552
Hello.


01:19:40.359 --> 01:19:41.475
Say something?


01:19:46.740 --> 01:19:48.151
Thank you.


01:19:51.495 --> 01:19:53.657
Sophie. Sophie!


01:20:00.671 --> 01:20:01.832
Okay.


01:20:05.843 --> 01:20:10.213
I never saw this, you know,
in my life so it's like, uh...


01:20:10.306 --> 01:20:11.592
Like, uh...


01:20:12.599 --> 01:20:14.010
What is this?


01:20:15.561 --> 01:20:19.225
Like real star, how can live
in this life, you know?


01:20:19.315 --> 01:20:21.398
Everybody recognize them, so...


01:20:24.611 --> 01:20:28.651
Okay, we can come there
and just give a couple sign, yeah?


01:20:28.741 --> 01:20:29.777
Okay, come on.


01:20:32.536 --> 01:20:35.870
I would like to see if they recognize
who I am, you know?


01:20:37.041 --> 01:20:38.953
- Shh! Shh! Shh!
- Please.


01:20:40.294 --> 01:20:42.001
You know who I am?


01:20:42.087 --> 01:20:43.953
Yeah!


01:20:44.048 --> 01:20:45.358
- Night King.
- The Night King.


01:20:45.382 --> 01:20:47.465
Aaah! Yes!


01:20:51.055 --> 01:20:52.657
- Where is my...?
- Winter is coming!


01:20:52.681 --> 01:20:55.389
Where is my army? Yes!


01:20:55.476 --> 01:20:57.684
I hope you win the war.


01:20:59.396 --> 01:21:01.103
You are the best, man.


01:21:02.191 --> 01:21:05.684
Hey, my friends, look at this.
Look at this. My lord.


01:21:05.778 --> 01:21:07.189
- Say something!
- What?


01:21:07.279 --> 01:21:08.395
- Say hi.
- Yeah! Hey!


01:21:08.489 --> 01:21:11.106
Yeah! <i>Game of Thr...</i>


01:21:15.162 --> 01:21:17.779
- Winter is coming!
- Winter is coming!


01:21:17.873 --> 01:21:20.616
Yeah! Yes!


01:22:09.466 --> 01:22:12.300
<i>That was Vlad the Night King's</i>


01:22:12.386 --> 01:22:15.129
<i>last-ever shot on</i> Game of Thrones.


01:22:52.593 --> 01:22:53.945
The best moment
for us is actually


01:22:53.969 --> 01:22:56.302
just before the cameras arrive...


01:22:57.306 --> 01:22:59.764
when we have it to ourselves
for a minute.


01:22:59.850 --> 01:23:04.686
When it's quiet, and you can feel
the set has a personality of its own,


01:23:04.771 --> 01:23:06.888
and it's all dressed and ready to go.


01:23:06.982 --> 01:23:08.518
That's when I love it.


01:23:10.068 --> 01:23:11.809
There's some mighty doors.


01:23:14.156 --> 01:23:15.897
Twenty-nine weeks, four days.


01:23:15.991 --> 01:23:18.233
Twenty-nine weeks,
four days.


01:23:18.327 --> 01:23:21.070
Not that you're counting.
Twenty-nine weeks.


01:23:21.163 --> 01:23:23.701
Still not bad
for seven months' work, Tom.


01:23:23.790 --> 01:23:26.203
You built a city in seven months.


01:23:29.713 --> 01:23:32.877
I honestly can say
I could not have worked harder.


01:23:32.966 --> 01:23:35.959
I really have given this
everything I have.


01:23:36.053 --> 01:23:40.047
And I love it when you see people
go up and they do this, you know?


01:23:45.646 --> 01:23:48.184
The minute that the camera arrives,
and the machines, and lights


01:23:48.273 --> 01:23:51.266
and hundreds of people come in,
they use it as they need to.


01:23:54.321 --> 01:23:55.983
We're quite shy people.


01:23:56.073 --> 01:23:58.440
We just wanna be able
to do our work and leave.


01:23:58.534 --> 01:24:01.277
I mean, I don't think the actors
would even know who I am.


01:24:01.370 --> 01:24:03.362
That suits me just fine.


01:24:16.718 --> 01:24:18.334
Well, I'm the carpet man.


01:24:18.428 --> 01:24:21.091
Well, apparently, there's
some looters coming.


01:24:21.807 --> 01:24:24.470
My scene is to frantically
bring the carpets in


01:24:24.560 --> 01:24:27.803
as quickly as I can, and get out
of the way and close the shutters.


01:24:27.896 --> 01:24:33.108
I've got the lovely maiden across
the way, trying to get her attention.


01:24:33.193 --> 01:24:34.684
She's otherwise occupied.


01:24:35.737 --> 01:24:37.777
Well, I'm just having a little
contemplative moment,


01:24:37.864 --> 01:24:39.446
enjoying the sunshine.


01:24:39.533 --> 01:24:41.866
And then...
Yeah, then all panic sets in.


01:24:41.952 --> 01:24:45.992
But I'm a bit precious about my pots,
you might have noticed.


01:24:46.081 --> 01:24:48.323
I kind of wanna get them all
off the balcony.


01:24:48.417 --> 01:24:49.703
Relax for a minute...


01:24:49.793 --> 01:24:51.312
<i>Can everyone hear me?</i>


01:24:51.336 --> 01:24:56.798
<i>You have to imagine right here today
that this is like alarms going off,</i>


01:24:56.883 --> 01:24:58.749
<i>there are air raid sirens.</i>


01:24:58.844 --> 01:25:02.804
<i>You guys are trying to get in
the Red Keep, which is over there.</i>


01:25:02.889 --> 01:25:06.178
<i>Welcome to King's Landing. Let's go.</i>


01:25:06.268 --> 01:25:08.134
- Action!
- And action.


01:25:09.479 --> 01:25:11.015
<i>Go, go, go.</i>


01:25:39.968 --> 01:25:41.834
<i>Good job, reset.</i>


01:25:44.181 --> 01:25:47.595
Golden Company, forward march!


01:25:47.684 --> 01:25:50.347
Left, right, left, right, left!


01:25:51.355 --> 01:25:52.391
Halt!


01:25:54.775 --> 01:25:56.311
First mark!


01:25:56.401 --> 01:25:59.439
- There's one, two, three...
- Oh, my God.


01:25:59.529 --> 01:26:03.022
Monday is four weeks away from
the end of principal photography.


01:26:03.116 --> 01:26:04.982
Oh, my God.


01:26:05.077 --> 01:26:06.443
How are your days looking?


01:26:06.536 --> 01:26:08.072
- Are they easing?
- No.


01:26:08.163 --> 01:26:11.782
No, we're actually in
probably almost...


01:26:11.875 --> 01:26:13.832
I wouldn't say
the toughest time, but...


01:26:13.919 --> 01:26:16.161
Not the way we all thought
we would have our...


01:26:16.254 --> 01:26:19.873
Spend our golden days
at <i>Game of Thrones.</i>


01:26:19.966 --> 01:26:21.548
What the fuck was I thinking?


01:26:21.635 --> 01:26:23.968
Which is what I'm gonna put
on my tombstone.


01:26:24.596 --> 01:26:26.303
Morning, morning.


01:26:26.390 --> 01:26:28.131
Ladies and gentlemen,
listen up!


01:26:28.225 --> 01:26:29.306
Listen up, guys!


01:26:29.393 --> 01:26:34.309
So as you all know, Sam and his team
have been rigging an explosion,


01:26:34.398 --> 01:26:38.267
and when we have shade,
we will blow this.


01:26:39.820 --> 01:26:41.580
Tonight,
we can stay there, right?


01:26:53.250 --> 01:26:56.084
Can you look after
Building 1, yeah?


01:26:56.169 --> 01:26:58.707
You know Building 1 outside the front?


01:26:58.797 --> 01:26:59.877
- Okay, yeah.
- Yeah?


01:26:59.923 --> 01:27:02.461
That's it then, guys.
Let's get to our stations.


01:27:02.551 --> 01:27:03.917
<i>Here we go.</i>


01:27:12.102 --> 01:27:13.468
Holy shit.


01:27:18.275 --> 01:27:20.002
We haven't had a chance
to look at it yet.


01:27:20.026 --> 01:27:21.767
We've only seen
the building site so far.


01:27:21.862 --> 01:27:25.481
It's the only place you can't wait
to watch all the men get burnt.


01:27:28.201 --> 01:27:29.658
There you go, cheers. Thank you.


01:27:29.745 --> 01:27:31.156
Okay, what can I get you?


01:27:32.330 --> 01:27:35.698
We've only got the wee ice lollies.
On the board you'll see all the ones.


01:27:38.170 --> 01:27:39.690
You can't beat the Pear Picking Porky.


01:27:41.590 --> 01:27:44.549
Completely cleaned out
the ice pops twice today.


01:27:44.634 --> 01:27:46.421
Never thought I was
gonna see this much heat,


01:27:46.511 --> 01:27:48.844
- feel this much heat.
- And complain about it so much.


01:27:48.930 --> 01:27:51.138
- And complain about it so much, yeah.
- Yeah.


01:27:51.224 --> 01:27:54.558
We like the cold.
We prefer the cold than the heat.


01:27:54.644 --> 01:27:56.055
Thank you so much.


01:28:01.485 --> 01:28:03.602
Free wave.


01:28:03.695 --> 01:28:05.402
That's brilliant,
you can turn them around,


01:28:05.489 --> 01:28:07.902
and somebody's up there
spinning it manically.


01:28:07.991 --> 01:28:10.950
There's gonna be
projectile vomit everywhere.


01:28:12.412 --> 01:28:14.199
I mean, you couldn't write it,
could you?


01:28:14.289 --> 01:28:18.750
Let's put a big, massive Ferris wheel,
and actually not tell anybody


01:28:18.835 --> 01:28:21.669
that we're putting
a Ferris wheel there.


01:28:21.755 --> 01:28:24.213
You know,
in amongst all the discussions


01:28:24.299 --> 01:28:27.758
about the big weekend, and our set
over there and filming there.


01:28:27.844 --> 01:28:30.632
Oh, no, they built
the fucking London Eye.


01:28:52.911 --> 01:28:54.402
- Cut there.
- Cut!


01:28:54.496 --> 01:28:56.954
- Reset, please.
- Reset!


01:28:58.500 --> 01:28:59.536
Oh, yeah.


01:29:00.544 --> 01:29:05.039
Do you know what
"club sandwich" means?


01:29:05.131 --> 01:29:07.373
- No.
- Chicken and lettuce under bacon,


01:29:07.467 --> 01:29:08.628
that's what that is.


01:29:08.718 --> 01:29:10.675
- I didn't know that.
- It's an acronym?


01:29:10.762 --> 01:29:12.549
Yeah, chicken and lettuce under bacon.


01:29:12.639 --> 01:29:13.699
Learn something new every day.


01:29:13.723 --> 01:29:15.305
Boom! Every day's
a schoolday, brother.


01:29:15.392 --> 01:29:17.634
- Rolling!
- And we're rolling.


01:29:17.727 --> 01:29:19.969
Rolling.
Let's be quiet, everyone.


01:29:39.499 --> 01:29:41.161
- Cut!
- Cut there.


01:29:41.251 --> 01:29:42.617
- Cut.
- Cut!


01:29:43.628 --> 01:29:45.439
Have we got a fake head
hanging around?


01:29:45.463 --> 01:29:47.671
Yup. Any severed head will do.


01:29:51.052 --> 01:29:54.762
Chow. Chow, why the fuck are you
wearing that Bolton jacket here?


01:29:54.848 --> 01:29:56.965
- What?
- Let me see this.


01:29:58.268 --> 01:30:00.496
- That's shite. Get out of here.
- What the fuck is this?


01:30:01.605 --> 01:30:03.767
How are you, man? You all right?
Nice, man.


01:30:03.857 --> 01:30:06.895
I'm not shaking your hand.


01:30:07.444 --> 01:30:09.606
Fucking Boltons, man.


01:30:09.696 --> 01:30:14.487
Hey, you didn't fucking think
about wearing that jacket, did you?


01:30:32.510 --> 01:30:34.547
<i>We're rolling, rolling.</i>


01:30:34.638 --> 01:30:37.346
As soon as they shout
"rolling," I'm preparing.


01:30:37.432 --> 01:30:40.345
"Action," I'm in Westeros.


01:30:41.394 --> 01:30:42.510
Action!


01:30:47.984 --> 01:30:50.692
You know, you can only
push a man so far, I think.


01:30:50.779 --> 01:30:53.396
You can only push his house so far.


01:30:53.490 --> 01:30:55.402
It doesn't matter how good he is,
you know?


01:30:55.492 --> 01:30:57.859
Their blood gets up. It's war.


01:30:59.788 --> 01:31:03.532
This is vengeance
for the Red Wedding, for the Starks.


01:31:03.625 --> 01:31:07.619
For seven seasons,
I've taken shit from House Lannister.


01:31:07.712 --> 01:31:10.455
So we're landing down in force,


01:31:10.548 --> 01:31:13.962
and we're just gonna kill everybody
inside the city.


01:31:14.052 --> 01:31:16.465
Unfortunately, for them.


01:31:50.797 --> 01:31:52.637
For the funeral scene,
it was all about


01:31:52.716 --> 01:31:55.049
blocking where everybody stands.


01:31:55.135 --> 01:31:57.047
That's why I work real hard
about preparation


01:31:57.137 --> 01:31:58.878
because I don't like
to waste people's time.


01:31:58.972 --> 01:32:01.589
And I wanna spend more time
directing actors.


01:32:01.683 --> 01:32:04.050
Are you this prepared
in all areas of your life?


01:32:04.144 --> 01:32:07.308
No. No, I'm not.


01:32:07.397 --> 01:32:10.856
If you saw my apartment this morning,
you'd see that


01:32:10.942 --> 01:32:13.730
that didn't get
any preparation at all.


01:32:13.820 --> 01:32:18.315
I have to have two cleaning ladies
come twice a week, it's so awful.


01:32:18.408 --> 01:32:19.774
It's such a mess.


01:32:22.120 --> 01:32:27.866
I want the journey to be
just as positive as the end product.


01:32:27.959 --> 01:32:29.791
That's important.


01:32:29.878 --> 01:32:31.870
Because what you remember
is the journey.


01:32:39.637 --> 01:32:42.254
...using all the fires and
get people in the foreground for us.


01:32:42.348 --> 01:32:46.137
We'll basically do
the eulogy, the speech,


01:32:46.227 --> 01:32:48.264
them all coming up to light the pyres,


01:32:48.354 --> 01:32:51.267
they all look at each other, then
drop down, light the pyre, and cut.


01:32:51.357 --> 01:32:54.566
We wanna match the last frame
of this to the first frame of that.


01:32:54.652 --> 01:32:57.645
Fill the frame and send it
to me and David Franco.


01:32:57.739 --> 01:32:59.659
- Good.
- Yeah, good. Morning, brother.


01:33:01.201 --> 01:33:03.784
- How are you?
- Good, brother. So you're just dead.


01:33:03.870 --> 01:33:06.110
- I'm dead. I'm dead.
- You're gonna do your death scene.


01:33:07.290 --> 01:33:09.452
Everyone wants a pied piper.


01:33:09.542 --> 01:33:12.535
Not to say that I'm the pied piper,
but I definitely can fake it.


01:33:13.963 --> 01:33:16.956
You create your own world
behind the camera.


01:33:17.050 --> 01:33:19.963
You're gonna take the pin out,
and you're reaching down here,


01:33:20.053 --> 01:33:23.967
and as you put it into his chest,
you then look at his eyes, like:


01:33:24.057 --> 01:33:26.265
- "You're a Stark now," right?
- Yeah.


01:33:26.351 --> 01:33:27.762
Then you stand up.


01:33:29.813 --> 01:33:31.999
- Okay. And then you go off right.
- Okay, cool.


01:33:32.023 --> 01:33:34.731
So just give me like
a couple minutes to get into it.


01:33:34.818 --> 01:33:36.796
- The way we just did it, right?
- Could we get


01:33:36.820 --> 01:33:39.403
everybody on their marks, please,
for the reference part?


01:33:39.489 --> 01:33:40.730
Feet here.


01:33:42.117 --> 01:33:45.610
Here you go, my brother. You're here.
A bunch of wildlings behind you.


01:33:45.703 --> 01:33:46.703
Good.


01:33:46.788 --> 01:33:48.404
If you guys can all meet him there...


01:33:48.498 --> 01:33:51.081
Yeah, I get pretty tired,
but I get invigorated, too.


01:33:51.167 --> 01:33:53.750
I guess sometimes
it's a bit of performance anxiety,


01:33:53.837 --> 01:33:56.830
where I wanna do a good job
so that everyone feels that:


01:33:56.923 --> 01:33:59.040
"Hey, he knows what he's doing."


01:33:59.134 --> 01:34:01.797
This is a dream job for a director.


01:34:01.886 --> 01:34:04.720
After directing Seasons 2, 3 and 5,


01:34:04.806 --> 01:34:07.549
I had to step away for
a couple seasons due to back issues.


01:34:07.642 --> 01:34:09.929
And I had a couple surgeries.


01:34:10.019 --> 01:34:12.227
So I missed it beyond belief.


01:34:12.313 --> 01:34:16.978
And coming back now,
I appreciate it so much that...


01:34:19.028 --> 01:34:20.860
this show saved my life.


01:34:23.700 --> 01:34:25.942
So, everybody, we're gonna
now talk about why we're here.


01:34:26.035 --> 01:34:29.244
Everyone here,
you've all lost mothers, brothers,


01:34:29.330 --> 01:34:31.868
and friends, and sisters,
and wives and everything.


01:34:31.958 --> 01:34:35.122
So background, it's all about playing
that attitude all the way through.


01:34:35.211 --> 01:34:36.452
Okay, ready? Here we go.


01:34:38.673 --> 01:34:41.290
My father died in a car accident
when I was a year and a half old


01:34:41.384 --> 01:34:42.841
so my mother and I grew up together.


01:34:42.927 --> 01:34:46.511
And she would listen to music,
and I'd sing and perform


01:34:46.598 --> 01:34:48.510
for her friends that
would come over for dinner.


01:34:49.642 --> 01:34:52.806
I wanted to be the next Barry Manilow.


01:34:52.896 --> 01:34:56.185
And then in college I realized that
wasn't really gonna happen for me


01:34:56.274 --> 01:34:57.936
so I said to myself,
"What else can I do?"


01:34:58.026 --> 01:35:03.067
And realized that my desire
to move people emotionally,


01:35:03.156 --> 01:35:05.773
I could do it by being involved
in filmmaking.


01:35:06.993 --> 01:35:08.200
Action.


01:35:18.004 --> 01:35:20.166
<i>Spirit move me</i>


01:35:20.256 --> 01:35:21.417
Can't go on?


01:35:21.507 --> 01:35:23.840
<i>Every time I'm near you</i>


01:35:25.511 --> 01:35:31.382
<i>Whirling like a cyclone in my mind</i>


01:35:31.768 --> 01:35:34.511
<i>Baby I love you, come</i>


01:35:35.855 --> 01:35:37.346
<i>Come</i>


01:35:37.899 --> 01:35:41.392
<i>Come into my arms</i>


01:35:42.070 --> 01:35:47.987
<i>Let me know the wonder of all of you</i>


01:35:48.076 --> 01:35:50.739
<i>Could it be magic now?</i>


01:35:50.828 --> 01:35:52.444
<i>Come on, come on</i>


01:35:52.538 --> 01:35:56.908
<i>Come, oh, come into my arms</i>


01:35:57.001 --> 01:36:01.245
<i>Oh, let me know the wonder</i>


01:36:01.339 --> 01:36:02.705
<i>Of all of you</i>


01:36:02.799 --> 01:36:07.043
<i>Oh, baby, I want you now, now</i>


01:36:07.136 --> 01:36:08.718
<i>Oh, now</i>


01:36:08.805 --> 01:36:12.594
<i>Oh, now and hold on fast</i>


01:36:12.684 --> 01:36:18.897
<i>Oh, could this be the magic at last?</i>


01:36:18.982 --> 01:36:21.190
<i>Could it be magic?</i>


01:36:29.492 --> 01:36:30.528
Now!


01:36:32.578 --> 01:36:34.114
Mr. David Nutter.


01:36:41.004 --> 01:36:45.339
The atmosphere today when we done
the big group photo, that hit home.


01:36:45.425 --> 01:36:48.759
I said goodbye to the Night's Watch.
I've known them for years.


01:36:51.764 --> 01:36:53.847
We all have extras jackets,


01:36:53.933 --> 01:36:56.926
and I managed to give
Kit Harington one today.


01:36:57.020 --> 01:36:59.683
And what's happened is, he's
now trying to give me money for it,


01:36:59.772 --> 01:37:00.888
but I won't take the money


01:37:00.982 --> 01:37:05.977
because I just want to give
Jon Snow his jacket, big time.


01:37:06.070 --> 01:37:09.108
So he'll never give me that money.
I don't want that money.


01:37:11.534 --> 01:37:13.651
It's gonna be very emotional
for the actors.


01:37:13.745 --> 01:37:17.864
I couldn't even imagine what it's
like for them to finally say goodbye.


01:37:27.675 --> 01:37:29.792
Babe.


01:37:29.886 --> 01:37:31.377
Aw.


01:37:31.471 --> 01:37:34.885
Oh, my God.


01:37:34.974 --> 01:37:37.432
We're in no rush this morning.


01:37:37.518 --> 01:37:40.101
No, I know, we're, you know...
You know what.


01:37:40.188 --> 01:37:42.931
But it's Emilia's last day,
we're in no rush.


01:37:46.736 --> 01:37:49.820
Is there any part of you
that's a bit relieved?


01:37:49.906 --> 01:37:51.738
- Do you know what I mean?
- Yeah.


01:37:52.700 --> 01:37:54.157
- Uh, yeah.
- Like, not in a:


01:37:54.243 --> 01:37:57.202
"Oh, thank fuck that's over,"
but as in...


01:37:58.581 --> 01:38:05.454
like a, "Oh, right, that's one thing
I don't need to panic about anymore."


01:38:05.546 --> 01:38:08.254
- I'm tired.
- Tired.


01:38:08.341 --> 01:38:12.176
I kind of had enough just now.


01:38:12.804 --> 01:38:15.638
- It's that bittersweet because...
- Yeah, exactly.


01:38:15.723 --> 01:38:17.305
...my life's been on pause.


01:38:17.392 --> 01:38:19.805
Let's unpause it
and get that garden fence painted.


01:38:19.894 --> 01:38:22.386
Exactly. Yeah, heaven's sake.


01:38:22.480 --> 01:38:25.223
Put that picture on the wall, damn it.


01:38:27.235 --> 01:38:29.898
But, yeah, that's definitely
an exhale of breath.


01:38:31.072 --> 01:38:32.563
So many people involved in this.


01:38:32.657 --> 01:38:35.775
You know,
it's just people's everything.


01:38:37.537 --> 01:38:39.824
It's kind of exciting
to sort of think:


01:38:39.914 --> 01:38:43.954
"Oh... Who am I without this, then...


01:38:44.043 --> 01:38:45.043
I wonder."


01:38:51.843 --> 01:38:53.004
Adjust.


01:38:54.929 --> 01:38:57.546
I'm trying to remember
the first time we put this thing on.


01:38:57.640 --> 01:39:00.929
I saw that...
A clip of that the other day,


01:39:01.018 --> 01:39:03.018
when you were riding
on that horse through Belfast,


01:39:03.104 --> 01:39:05.141
and it was absolutely freezing.


01:39:05.231 --> 01:39:07.644
And you were, like,
in nothing but a slip.


01:39:07.733 --> 01:39:08.814
Yeah.


01:39:09.652 --> 01:39:12.565
- No such thing as thermals back then.
- Whew.


01:39:20.538 --> 01:39:24.908
I'm not sure this wig's got
much more life left in it.


01:39:25.001 --> 01:39:28.165
Neither has the head
underneath it, so...


01:39:29.505 --> 01:39:31.462
Oh! It's the last time.


01:39:31.549 --> 01:39:33.165
That's the last time.


01:39:34.135 --> 01:39:36.718
Oh, that's really weird.


01:39:56.115 --> 01:39:57.322
<i>Gimme the ring</i>


01:39:58.743 --> 01:40:00.530
<i>Kissed and told</i>


01:40:00.620 --> 01:40:02.282
<i>Gimme something that I missed</i>


01:40:05.500 --> 01:40:10.120
<i>A hand to hold
Wild and what it seems</i>


01:40:10.213 --> 01:40:11.545
<i>Gimme the ring</i>


01:40:12.465 --> 01:40:13.876
<i>Kill the king</i>


01:40:14.800 --> 01:40:16.541
<i>When love is the law</i>


01:40:16.636 --> 01:40:18.298
<i>Gimme the ring</i>


01:40:18.930 --> 01:40:20.171
<i>Gimme dream child</i>


01:40:20.264 --> 01:40:21.425
Right.


01:40:21.516 --> 01:40:24.554
<i>Do you hear me call?
Gimme the ring</i>


01:40:26.145 --> 01:40:27.727
<i>On the loan</i>


01:40:28.231 --> 01:40:30.439
<i>Still on the floor</i>


01:40:30.525 --> 01:40:32.733
<i>Gimme the ring</i>


01:40:32.818 --> 01:40:34.605
<i>Sing dream child</i>


01:40:35.321 --> 01:40:37.153
<i>Do you hear me at all?</i>


01:40:38.741 --> 01:40:41.654
That was Emilia's last shot
on <i>Game of Thrones.</i>


01:40:48.501 --> 01:40:51.460
Yeah, this is my idea of hell,
at the moment.


01:40:51.546 --> 01:40:53.879
I hate goodbyes anyway,
I'm not good at it.


01:40:53.965 --> 01:40:57.333
I'll try to just sneak out
the back door and miss this bit out.


01:41:16.988 --> 01:41:19.605
Ah, here's a bit of wood
I could take home.


01:41:23.953 --> 01:41:26.787
That's where we stabbed Jon Snow.


01:41:26.872 --> 01:41:28.955
We'll never forget that one.


01:41:32.169 --> 01:41:35.128
Well, old girl, cheerio.


01:41:35.214 --> 01:41:36.830
You served us well.


01:41:38.509 --> 01:41:39.750
Sleep tight.


01:41:53.274 --> 01:41:54.274
Okay.


01:41:54.358 --> 01:41:56.315
Now I've got
everything packed to take.


01:42:25.640 --> 01:42:28.223
It's just fucking tele, isn't it?


01:42:29.060 --> 01:42:30.676
Oh, it is.


01:42:30.770 --> 01:42:35.686
Obviously this has been
really quite hard.


01:42:35.775 --> 01:42:38.142
And, um, I think,


01:42:38.235 --> 01:42:41.148
you know, some days we've
really struggled to get through it.


01:42:41.238 --> 01:42:43.730
And I think if it wasn't
for you guys and your morale,


01:42:43.824 --> 01:42:45.986
that's really what has got us through.


01:42:46.077 --> 01:42:47.304
But this is obviously a big end.


01:42:47.328 --> 01:42:49.991
I know lots of you are going home
as of the weekend.


01:42:50.081 --> 01:42:53.950
I hope that we get
other projects like this again.


01:42:54.043 --> 01:42:55.875
I don't.


01:42:56.837 --> 01:42:58.999
Because I wanna keep
the team together.


01:42:59.090 --> 01:43:01.628
So thank you, everybody. Thank you.


01:43:10.101 --> 01:43:12.639
So it's me, you, Big Johnny.


01:43:12.728 --> 01:43:15.095
- Shane Cavanaugh's coming in, too.
- All right. Nice.


01:43:15.189 --> 01:43:17.397
I heard it's only 12 people doing it.


01:43:17.483 --> 01:43:19.850
Yeah, there's only 10 Unsullied.


01:43:21.612 --> 01:43:22.898
You all right, man?


01:43:22.988 --> 01:43:25.526
- Yeah.
- There's very few of us in for this.


01:43:25.616 --> 01:43:26.652
I was just told


01:43:26.742 --> 01:43:28.825
I have a feature
there at the very last episode.


01:43:28.911 --> 01:43:31.494
So Jon's honor guard.
I was like, "No way." So...


01:43:31.580 --> 01:43:34.197
Do you think
you'll get seen on camera?


01:43:34.291 --> 01:43:35.657
Um...


01:43:35.751 --> 01:43:40.837
Because it's such a tight scene
with less numbers,


01:43:40.923 --> 01:43:43.506
possibly, yeah. Yeah. So, um...


01:43:44.802 --> 01:43:48.762
Yeah, it'll be like, yeah,
just point to me:


01:43:48.848 --> 01:43:50.259
"Dad, there I am. Look, again."


01:43:50.349 --> 01:43:53.342
And he'll be like,
"Yup. Again."


01:43:53.644 --> 01:43:56.978
So it would be a brilliant way
to cap off a season.


01:43:57.064 --> 01:44:01.525
In 2016, 2015.


01:44:03.779 --> 01:44:07.614
I'm trying to find
Andy McClay's first day.


01:44:08.701 --> 01:44:10.442
Ah, there he is.


01:44:10.536 --> 01:44:12.778
This is the first makeup look.


01:44:12.872 --> 01:44:15.615
I was like, "You'll never get a part
if you look like that.


01:44:15.708 --> 01:44:17.791
You'll have to change
your expression."


01:44:17.877 --> 01:44:20.369
And then we got Andy McClay.


01:44:20.463 --> 01:44:22.204
Cold Andy.


01:44:23.382 --> 01:44:24.998
It's as if it's day one.


01:44:25.092 --> 01:44:29.712
You had come in and you told me
that your house had just burnt down.


01:44:29.805 --> 01:44:31.575
- Oh, yeah, fire in the house.
- And I was like:


01:44:31.599 --> 01:44:34.808
- "And you're here for a makeup test?"
- Had the fire in the house, yeah.


01:44:34.894 --> 01:44:36.055
You weren't late either.


01:44:36.145 --> 01:44:38.512
No, I wasn't late.
This is the thing, man.


01:44:38.606 --> 01:44:41.815
Escape from the reality.


01:44:43.903 --> 01:44:45.360
- Right.
- Look there, now.


01:44:46.697 --> 01:44:47.983
- Got you.
- Sorted.


01:44:48.073 --> 01:44:50.030
- Off you pop, off you pop.
- Goodbye, Andy.


01:44:50.117 --> 01:44:51.358
Off you pop.


01:44:54.371 --> 01:44:57.284
So it's sinking in now,
that it's my last day.


01:44:59.543 --> 01:45:03.287
Just back to normal life now
after this.


01:45:08.636 --> 01:45:10.798
Good morning, how are you?
Nice to see you.


01:45:10.888 --> 01:45:11.924
Good morning.


01:45:15.601 --> 01:45:16.933
Kit, all right, man.


01:45:18.354 --> 01:45:20.562
Ah, nice one, man. Nice one, man.


01:45:22.233 --> 01:45:24.520
Do you want a Season 8 one?


01:45:24.610 --> 01:45:27.603
A Targaryen dragon man
with a direwolf head in the middle,


01:45:27.696 --> 01:45:29.216
that's what we're getting
for Season 8.


01:45:30.115 --> 01:45:31.276
Yeah, yeah, yeah.


01:45:32.660 --> 01:45:34.868
Yeah? We can get you one of them
if you want one.


01:45:36.121 --> 01:45:37.828
Yeah, man. Yeah. Some details...


01:45:41.377 --> 01:45:42.377
Yeah, yeah.


01:45:43.587 --> 01:45:48.048
- Sweet, man. Nice one. Sweet, eh?
- See you.


01:45:49.426 --> 01:45:51.634
- I know, man. I know.
- Last day.


01:45:52.304 --> 01:45:54.466
Aw... What?


01:45:59.061 --> 01:46:02.304
In the name of the one true queen,
Daenerys Targaryen...


01:46:03.607 --> 01:46:05.143
I sentence you to die.


01:46:05.234 --> 01:46:06.270
Grey Worm.


01:46:07.111 --> 01:46:08.818
Grey Worm, he's totally gone.


01:46:08.904 --> 01:46:10.770
And of course
Jon's trying to save lives


01:46:10.865 --> 01:46:13.858
so him and Grey Worm
have a standoff there.


01:46:13.951 --> 01:46:15.567
I think that the Starks
in the background


01:46:15.661 --> 01:46:19.621
are in a very precarious situation
because we hate Lannisters.


01:46:22.042 --> 01:46:23.874
We don't care if they die.


01:46:23.961 --> 01:46:26.203
But it's our king's command.


01:46:26.297 --> 01:46:28.960
And if the Unsullied
are pointing their spears at him,


01:46:29.049 --> 01:46:31.006
- we're not happy with that.
- Easy!


01:46:31.093 --> 01:46:34.302
Set. Three, two, one, action.


01:46:54.825 --> 01:46:56.737
- Cut.
- Okay, cut there.


01:46:58.454 --> 01:47:01.162
So with that,
that is a <i>Game of Thrones</i> wrap


01:47:01.248 --> 01:47:05.868
on our good friend Jacob Anderson,
Liam Cunningham and Kit Harington.


01:47:05.961 --> 01:47:07.577
Keet!


01:47:07.671 --> 01:47:09.333
Keet!


01:47:09.423 --> 01:47:11.380
Keet!


01:47:11.467 --> 01:47:15.336
Ten years ago,
you walked into Nina Gold's office,


01:47:15.429 --> 01:47:17.011
as a 12-year-old...


01:47:19.600 --> 01:47:22.013
...and here we are now.


01:47:22.102 --> 01:47:23.764
Your watch has ended,


01:47:23.854 --> 01:47:28.189
and it has been a hell of a watch.


01:47:28.275 --> 01:47:32.815
For us, for these people and for
so many people around the world.


01:47:32.905 --> 01:47:34.316
Thank you for being Jon Snow


01:47:34.406 --> 01:47:36.898
and thank you more than that
for being you.


01:47:41.789 --> 01:47:44.623
I feel
that my heart is breaking.


01:47:44.708 --> 01:47:46.324
I love this show...


01:47:49.463 --> 01:47:52.171
more than, I think, anything.


01:47:52.257 --> 01:47:55.216
It has never been a job for me.


01:47:55.302 --> 01:47:57.464
It's been my life,
and this will always be


01:47:57.554 --> 01:48:00.718
the greatest thing I'll ever do
and be a part of.


01:48:00.808 --> 01:48:04.176
And you have been just my family.


01:48:04.269 --> 01:48:06.682
I love you for it,
and thank you so much.


01:48:17.241 --> 01:48:18.527
Reset, please.


01:48:30.504 --> 01:48:31.836
Thanks, man.


01:48:38.554 --> 01:48:41.388
I'm choking up here, man.
Honestly.


01:48:41.473 --> 01:48:42.473
Um...


01:48:43.517 --> 01:48:46.055
It's what Kit was saying. Um...


01:48:47.604 --> 01:48:52.269
Even though, uh...
I'm just an extra...


01:48:54.069 --> 01:48:58.484
in comparison to him
being the main star, um...


01:48:59.825 --> 01:49:03.193
it has... It really has
changed my life.


01:49:03.287 --> 01:49:06.997
The show... I didn't
think I was gonna get this emotional.


01:49:07.082 --> 01:49:08.948
It has, it really has.


01:49:09.043 --> 01:49:12.127
Well, the past five years has been
the best five years...


01:49:12.796 --> 01:49:15.584
It's been the best five years
of my life, like,


01:49:15.674 --> 01:49:17.256
so I will miss it.


01:49:17.342 --> 01:49:20.301
But it's always something that I'll
be able to look back on, man, so...


01:49:22.347 --> 01:49:24.714
Absolutely brilliant. It's just...


01:49:24.808 --> 01:49:28.677
It's hard to fathom that I'll never
be coming back to <i>Game of Thrones.</i>


01:49:28.771 --> 01:49:31.104
- So, but...
- Back to the TEC. Going this way.


01:49:31.190 --> 01:49:32.601
Best thing I've ever done.


01:49:34.318 --> 01:49:37.436
<i>There are four white walls</i>


01:49:37.529 --> 01:49:39.737
<i>In every damn hotel</i>


01:49:39.823 --> 01:49:43.783
<i>A light by the bed
Stains on the floor</i>


01:49:43.869 --> 01:49:48.364
<i>And it's here
I will wait out the storm</i>


01:49:48.457 --> 01:49:50.377
It's hard saying goodbye
to everybody.


01:49:51.502 --> 01:49:55.621
There's too many people
that you just wanna talk to


01:49:55.714 --> 01:49:58.878
and say how much you love them
and thank them, and you just can't.


01:50:00.135 --> 01:50:02.001
I think that I was able to...


01:50:03.472 --> 01:50:10.265
I don't know,
to bring my philosophy of,


01:50:10.354 --> 01:50:15.395
you know, love, and camaraderie
and family to the show.


01:50:15.484 --> 01:50:18.693
You know, that's the way
I just always treat everybody.


01:50:20.280 --> 01:50:22.988
Now, if people have <i>Game of Thrones</i>
on their credits,


01:50:23.075 --> 01:50:26.034
people know that person
had to work really hard,


01:50:26.120 --> 01:50:27.952
that person knew what they were doing,


01:50:28.038 --> 01:50:32.203
that person created,
you know, a magical world.


01:50:36.296 --> 01:50:38.709
<i>There are red velvet seats</i>


01:50:38.799 --> 01:50:41.291
<i>In the windowless rooms</i>


01:50:41.385 --> 01:50:43.798
<i>A curtain to draw</i>


01:50:43.887 --> 01:50:45.844
<i>Faces to please</i>


01:50:45.931 --> 01:50:51.677
<i>And it's here
I will wait out the storm</i>


01:50:51.770 --> 01:50:56.105
<i>Killing time
On the fringes again</i>


01:50:57.317 --> 01:50:59.855
<i>Before the leaving</i>


01:51:02.322 --> 01:51:05.030
<i>Before the leaving</i>


01:51:21.133 --> 01:51:22.777
Ladies and gentlemen,


01:51:22.801 --> 01:51:25.259
welcome to <i>Game of Thrones</i> tours.


01:51:25.345 --> 01:51:28.133
What is dead may never die,


01:51:28.223 --> 01:51:33.389
but rises again, harder and stronger.


01:51:33.478 --> 01:51:34.622
So, guys, you're very welcome


01:51:34.646 --> 01:51:36.040
to the <i>Game of Thrones</i> tours.


01:51:36.064 --> 01:51:37.600
I'm gonna be talking about this.


01:51:37.691 --> 01:51:39.648
This is Carrick Castle.


01:51:39.735 --> 01:51:43.149
Guys, Carrick Castle
is not in <i>Game of Thrones</i>


01:51:43.238 --> 01:51:44.299
so we're just gonna fucking


01:51:44.323 --> 01:51:45.800
drive on past Carrick Castle.


01:51:45.824 --> 01:51:48.191
And I'm gonna take you
to Stannis's camp.


01:51:48.285 --> 01:51:51.778
Right, what we're gonna see is all
the lads laying low for their gruel,


01:51:51.872 --> 01:51:53.704
then who's gonna pop on?


01:51:53.790 --> 01:51:57.454
It's Ser Davos Seaworth,
Hand of the King to Stannis Baratheon,


01:51:57.544 --> 01:51:59.285
easing himself onto camera.


01:51:59.379 --> 01:52:02.213
That's me right there. Brrr!


01:52:02.299 --> 01:52:04.586
Wasn't even cold that day on set.


01:52:04.676 --> 01:52:07.293
Acting, is what we call this.


01:52:07.387 --> 01:52:09.299
Yeah? All right.


01:52:09.389 --> 01:52:13.599
Here we come, we're coming around
the corner and we're gonna see...


01:52:13.685 --> 01:52:15.142
Irish mists.


01:52:15.229 --> 01:52:19.348
And we're coming up here now,
just around this bend.


01:52:19.441 --> 01:52:21.774
Castle Black, ladies and gentlemen.


01:52:21.860 --> 01:52:23.772
I guarantee that it is up there.


01:52:23.862 --> 01:52:25.945
If you could see it, well done to you.


01:52:26.031 --> 01:52:28.273
This American guy said to me, he said:


01:52:29.326 --> 01:52:33.070
"Hey. Hey, buddy." And I was like,
"Yeah, what's up, man?"


01:52:33.163 --> 01:52:38.283
He said, "How did the trouble start?
Tell me, how did the trouble start?"


01:52:38.377 --> 01:52:41.165
And I was like, "Well, mate,
the troubles first started


01:52:41.255 --> 01:52:43.747
when Jaime Lannister
pushed Bran Stark out a window."

